<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean gold imports/exports soar in Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>S.Korean gold imports/exports soar in Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's gold imports for the first 11 months of this year totalled $4.74 billion, up 100.8 percent from $2.36 billion for the same period of 1995, the Finance Ministry said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Gold exports during the same 11-month period rose 103.7 percent to $4.42 billion from $2.17 billion worth of imports for the comparable period in 1995, it said.  </p>
<p>In volume, gold imports totalled 374.7 tonnes for the January-November period, up 99.2 percent from 188.1 tonnes imported in the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Gold exports for the period stood at 350.7 tonnes, up 100.9 percent from 174.6 tonnes a year earlier, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
